# W1 (Platform slice 2, write IO): stdout/stderr are pre-open WRITE Handles, and
# $h.write($s) writes raw text with NO trailing newline (unlike print/note). This
# fixture proves the WRITE-TIME wrapper: the differential gate redirects the
# interpreter's stdout via SetOutput AFTER the prelude binds `stdout`, and the
# stdoutWriter wrapper resolves ev.out at write time, so these writes are still
# captured (not leaked to the real stdout). Interleaving print (which appends a
# newline) shows write appends none, and the bare form write(stdout, $s) lowers
# the same as the method form $h.write($s).
sub main(): Int {
    stdout.write("a")
    stdout.write("b")
    print("")
    write(stdout, "c")
    stdout.write("d\n")
    print("done")
    0
}
